10]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>ABSTRACT<\/jats:title><jats:p>We propose a model of dynamic investment, financing, and risk management for financially constrained firms. The model highlights the central importance of the endogenous marginal value of liquidity (cash and credit line) for corporate decisions. Our three main results are: (1) investment depends on the ratio of marginal\u2002<jats:italic>q<\/jats:italic>\u2002to the marginal value of liquidity, and the relation between investment and marginal\u2002<jats:italic>q<\/jats:italic>\u2002changes with the marginal source of funding; (2) optimal external financing and payout are characterized by an endogenous double\u2010barrier policy for the firm's cash\u2010capital ratio; and (3) liquidity management and derivatives hedging are complementary risk management tools.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1111\/j.1540-6261.2011.01681.x","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2011,9,24]],"date-time":"2011-09-24T02:29:43Z","timestamp":1316831383000},"page":"1545-1578","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":624,"title":["A Unified Theory of Tobin's\u2002<i>q<\/i>, Corporate Investment, Financing, and Risk Management"],"prefix":"10.1111","volume":"66","author":[{"given":"PATRICK","family":"BOLTON","sequence":"first","affiliation":[]},{"given":"HUI","family":"CHEN","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[]},{"given":"NENG","family":"WANG","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2011,9,21]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_9_2_1","first-page":"228","article-title":"Optimal investment under uncertainty","volume":"73","author":"Abel Andrew B.","year":"1983","journal-title":"American Economic Review"},{"key":"e_1_2_9_3_1","first-page":"1369","article-title":"A unified model of investment under uncertainty","volume":"84","author":"Abel Andrew B.","year":"1994","journal-title":"American Economic Review"},{"key":"e_1_2